WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.380
Show your work, sell with confidence, and plan your growth.

2
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:07.650
This is the video for module 4 of Fashion Business Management.

3
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:17.520
Most fashion clients now decide whether to contact a tailor after seeing her work on WhatsApp status, a catalogue or Instagram.

4
00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:27.800
You do not need a professional photographer. You need clear, honest photos of your real work, organised so a client finds what she wants quickly.

5
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:33.980
Then you learn to talk about value, take payments safely, and plan your next three months.

6
00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:43.500
Shoot in daylight near a window, not in harsh midday sun or yellow bulb light. Use a plain background so the outfit stands out.

7
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:54.010
Take the full front, back and side, and close-ups of the neckline, sleeve and the inside finishing. Clothes look best worn, with the client's permission.

8
00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:03.860
Wipe the lens and hold the phone steady. Crop and brighten if needed, but never change colours or shape. She must receive what she saw.

9
00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:12.400
WhatsApp Business is a free app. Use a separate line if you can, and put your one-sentence business statement in your profile.

10
00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:22.120
Add your best 10 to 20 garments, and group them into collections such as office wear or owambe styles. Put your most typical work first.

11
00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:30.200
Save quick replies for your price guide and terms, and use labels like new order, deposit paid and ready.

12
00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:42.570
Always ask before posting a client, and respect a no. Never post measurements, phone numbers or addresses, and blur children's faces unless a parent agrees in writing.

13
00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:50.410
Clients ask the same questions: how much, how long, can you make it in my size? Answer them in the entry.

14
00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:55.450
Kemi shows the front and back, plus close-ups of the lined, overlocked inside.

15
00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:05.020
Her prices come from her costing sheet: from 25,000 naira with the client's fabric, and from 48,000 for the full package.

16
00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:16.380
She adds: ready in 10 days after deposit and fitting, with one free adjustment within 7 days. Her chats now move faster from question to deposit.

17
00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:27.470
Clients rarely pay for stitches. They pay for how they look at the event, and for confidence it will be ready. When you only talk price, they compare only cost.

18
00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:36.670
So talk about fit, finish, reliability and aftercare. When she says please reduce it, never go below your total cost.

19
00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:44.130
Say, I can do it at 35,000 without the lining. Or keep the price and add value, like a matching headwrap.

20
00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:50.260
Group orders need a written proposal. Blessing starts from her real costing sheet.

21
00:02:51.510 --> 00:03:03.760
Her cost is about 14,000 per gown. For a bulk order she takes a 20% margin: 14,000 divided by 0.8 is 17,500 naira.

22
00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:13.630
She can finish about 10 gowns a week, so she quotes 3 weeks. She asks for a 50% deposit, with all measurements by a fixed date.

23
00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:29.730
The whole order is 525,000 naira. Her one-page proposal lists style, price, deposit, timeline, fittings and alteration policy. Never fund a large order from your own pocket without a deposit.

24
00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:36.950
Watch for payment scams. Confirm every payment in your app, never from an alert or screenshot.

25
00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:49.370
If someone overpays and asks for a refund, wait until the money clears, and refund only to the same account. No real bank will ask for your PIN, password or OTP.

26
00:03:50.620 --> 00:04:02.310
For example, Ada in Onitsha plans one focus per month, each with a number to check. First, she fixes pricing, because growth on weak pricing only multiplies losses.

27
00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:08.510
Next, she builds sales with regular posts, new catalogue items and reviews.

28
00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:18.570
Then she trains her apprentice, freeing about 5 hours a week. On day 90 she writes a report comparing results with before the course.

29
00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:27.080
To remember. Show real work honestly. Answer questions before they are asked. Protect your margin and your money.

30
00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:33.740
To earn your certificate, submit your capstone evidence and score at least 70% in the final quiz.

31
00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:41.950
Your turn. Launch your catalogue, prepare your sales toolkit, and assemble your evidence pack and 90-day plan.

32
00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.240
Continue with the lessons below.
